# Outer verification · `guide:verification:outer-consumer`

**Section (Verification)** · `sec:verification:area-verification` {{ row('org.peer-network.testing.claim-areas', owner='VERIFICATION', area='verification').stake }} pn-verification is unpublished development support with no production dependencies. Its tests consume pn-records through public APIs and the records test-support feature, using the same input generator with a verification-owned fixed-point closure oracle and exact-cause table. This is a second observation of the same implementation, not an independent implementation; the outer expectations do not call the inner predicates or use the generator's returned expected error.

**Implementation remark (Outer consumer)** · `impl:verification:outer-consumer` The conformance roster records each exact typed refusal and overlapping-closure case through pn-testkit. Consumer-qualified source-v1 seeds and 256 generated cases per property are joined to the current source and configuration. Replay uses `PROPTEST_RNG_SEED` with `cargo test --locked -p pn-verification --test properties`, with other PROPTEST variables and `PN_PROPERTY_SEED_PN_VERIFICATION` unset; proptest shrinks the word vectors and persists minimized failures in proptest-regressions. The crate does not admit acts, partition closures, verify signatures or provide real services. Bite 11 extends this outer consumer.

**Amendment (Bite 1 public evidence)** · `amend:verification:bite-one-evidence` The supported premises for (`[ROOT-gate:design:bite-1]`) are: Finite structural, act-removal, whole-history, canonical dependency and asserted-parent, opaque declaration and outside-history causal closure-input fixtures, with local unit/public/integration levels, shared conformance, recorded inner and outer properties and runtime outcomes; no partition, family formation or declaration payload semantics is claimed. Evidence is (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:identity-is-structural]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:complete-acts-are-counted-once]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:duplicates-refuse-and-parallel-identities-survive]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:both-co-legs-are-required]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:protocol-references-outlive-dependency-removal]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:invalid-local-fields-refuse]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:removal-belongs-to-act-projections]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:references-resolve-against-accepted-history]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:opaque-editions-preserve-as-of-selection]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:ambiguous-declaration-histories-refuse]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:dependency-lists-have-canonical-content]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:dependencies-require-earlier-accepted-acts]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:history-owns-its-structural-references]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:overlapping-closures-retain-complete-inputs]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:incomplete-boundary-inputs-refuse]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:asserted-parents-are-canonical-and-earlier]`), (`[ROOT-claim:discipline:records-entry-is-observed-without-changing-results]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:generated-closures-match-independent-search]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:single-corruptions-retain-typed-causes]`), (`[RECORDS-claim:acts:shared-conformance-preserves-whole-acts]`), (`claim:verification:generated-closures-match-independent-search`), (`claim:verification:single-corruptions-retain-typed-causes`), (`claim:verification:shared-conformance-preserves-whole-acts`), (`[ROOT-claim:discipline:generated-records-refusals-retain-outcomes]`), (`[TESTKIT-claim:testkit:recorded-seed-replays-a-shrunk-failure]`). This outer-consumer paragraph aggregates the inner and outer witnesses without a reverse dependency from records to verification. The complete bite was independently admitted in (`[ROOT-amend:decomposition:bite-one-admission]`); the later partition and parameter holds remain explicit.

**Amendment (Outer numeric observation)** · `amend:verification:numeric-observation` The shared records-numerics-1 inputs exercise the same pn-records implementation through an outer-owned integer cross-product oracle and typed refusal table. (`claim:verification:generated-numeric-coordinates-retain-their-laws`) and (`claim:verification:shared-numeric-cases-preserve-exact-contracts`) retain the consumer-qualified source-v1 seed and configured case count; they do not duplicate the inner expectation function or claim a second implementation. Repricing with a fixed numeraire changes reduced quantities; recoinage co-expresses the numeraire. Wider generators, fence evaluation and real-service evidence remain in their owning slices.

**Amendment (Outer burn recognition cases)** · `amend:verification:burn-recognition` The outer consumer executes records-burn-1 through pn-records public APIs with its own exact-cause table, a consumer-qualified seed and the shared shrinkable fixture inputs. (`claim:verification:shared-marker-cases-preserve-recognition-contracts`) and (`claim:verification:generated-marker-corruptions-retain-typed-causes`) establish a second observation of the pure recognition premises, not a second implementation or proof of external destruction, finality or commitment cryptography.
